# Live viewer stability

- Ports `8889` and `8890` are persistent user-facing viewer services.
- Both must expose exactly these pages/tabs: `Original viewer`, `Pipeline`, and
  `GPT Image 2 vs Gemini`.
- The live pages are pinned under `run/locked_viewers/`. Do not edit, rebuild,
  replace, or delete those snapshots unless the user explicitly asks to change
  the live format.
- Do not stop or replace the `layoutgen-viewers` tmux session. Its two watchdog
  loops automatically restart either server if it exits.
- Viewer development must write to a different output file or use a different
  port. Editing source files or ordinary `results/*.html` artifacts must not
  affect the live pages.
- After relevant work, verify `/`, `/pipeline`, and `/comparison` return HTTP
  200 on both ports without changing their navigation.
